{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>והיה לכם למשמרת.</b> That each person shall keep it in his house." "<b>בין הערבים.</b> A difficult word. R. Solomon said that it is the moment of the sun's inclination from midday toward the west, but he gave no reason why [it says] ערבים in the plural. Now it is written: ובהעלות אהרן את הנרות בין הערבים (below, 30:8), and there is no doubt that he lights the lamps at sunset. And when we searched this word we found that the moment between the evenings is called ערב, for thus it is written: בין הערבים תאכלו בשר (Exodus 16:12), and there it is written: בתת ה׳ לכם בערב בשר לאכול (ibid. 8). And regarding the lighting of the lamps it is written: יערוך אותו אהרן ובניו מערב עד בקר (Exodus 27:21). And it is written: עולות לה׳ לבקר ולערב (Ezra 3:3). And it is written: ואת הכבש השני תעשה בין הערבים (below, 29:39). Now concerning the Passover, regarding which בין הערבים is written, we found: שם תזבח את הפסח בערב כבא השמש מועד צאתך ממצרים (Deut. 16:6) — the meaning is: when the sun comes to the side of the west, and this does not signify arrival, for it is the opposite of the sun's going out, as it is written: השמש יצא על הארץ (Gen. 19:23), that it began to appear upon the earth, and likewise: ובא השמש וטהר (Lev. 22:7), that it no longer appears upon the earth. Now it is written concerning nocturnal emission: והיה לפנות ערב ירחץ במים (Deut. 23:12). And if the matter is not so, let them explain to us what difference there is between כבא השמש of the Passover and כבא השמש of nocturnal emission, and likewise ובא השמש וטהר (Lev. 22:7). The heretics said that there are three evenings, and their proof is because they found: עד הערב השלישית (I Sam. 20:5). But they did not recognize the truth and did not understand, for it is written: מחר חדש ... ושלשת תרד מאוד (ibid. 19), whose meaning is: when the third day from the day adjacent to the evening of the field where you are hiding comes — and therefore he said עד הערב השלישי.\n\nAnd now I return to explain. Know that the pattern of ערבים always falls on the dual pattern, like אָבְנָיִם (above, 1:16) and like לוחֹתָיִם (Ezek. 27:5), and likewise דְּרָכַיִם (Prov. 28:6) — and the witness falls on one (ibid.) — and likewise שמים, for they are the two plates of the sphere, which are like driven pegs on which the sphere rests, and likewise לנטוע שמים (Isa. 51:16). And I already explained in the Book of the Great Name that שמים is from the root שם, ישר נכח עמו (Job 23:7) — an allusion to two places. Now we have two evenings: one is the sun's evening, and that is the time of its entry beneath the earth; and the second is the arrival of its light that appears in the clouds. And between them is approximately an hour and a third of an hour. Then a man with emission comes to the camp and Aaron lights the lamps.\n\nSaid the Gaon [Saadia], may his memory be blessed: The measure of the altar of burnt offering is five cubits length and five cubits width, and by this measure only a few priests could stand, who toss the blood of the Passover offerings before it coagulates. Now in the days of Josiah, when Israel were few, the priests could not toss the blood of the Passover and peace offerings — to toss them within an hour and a third of an hour — all the more so when all the tribes were in their land. Now there was a tradition that they would begin to slaughter from the moment when it becomes clear to a person that the sun has inclined toward the west. And Scripture mentioned בין הערבים because most of the Passover offerings were slaughtered then, and it is the end of the time that must not pass until the evening of the sun's light."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The first citation of I Sam. 20:5 is given as (ש״א ב, ה), apparently a typo for (ש״א כ, ה); the second citation is given as (שם שם יה י״ט), where 'יה' is a numeral abbreviation for 15 (= chapter 20 in Hebrew verse numbering conventions) alongside 'י״ט' for verse 19, though the reference seems garbled in the witnesses; translated as (ibid. 19) following context."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:43.993343590Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}